      "page_title": "Type Assertions and Type Switches",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Type Switch Shape"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "switch v := i.(type) {",
            "case int:        use(v) // v is int",
            "case int, int64: use(v) // v stays any",
            "case nil:        // nil interface value",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`case nil` is distinct from an interface holding a nil pointer",
            "Duplicate cases are a compile error",
            "No `fallthrough`, unlike an expression switch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Capability Upgrades"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "if wt, ok := w.(io.WriterTo); ok {",
            "\treturn wt.WriteTo(dst) // fast path",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Exactly how `io.Copy` skips the buffer round trip",
            "`errors.As` is the assertion for wrapped error chains",
            "`errors.Is` compares against sentinel values"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Assertion Price"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Target",
            "Work done"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "concrete type",
              "pointer compare"
            ],
            [
              "interface type",
              "itab lookup, cached"
            ],
            [
              "nil interface",
              "immediate false"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When Not To"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A long switch over your own types: add a method instead",
            "Legit: decoding `any` from JSON, error inspection",
            "Legit: capability upgrades and generic-ish helpers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Assert to `error` or to `*MyErr`?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`error` — any type implementing it matches",
            "`*MyErr` — only that exact concrete type",
            "Wrapped chains need `errors.As`, not a bare assert"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "var me *MyErr",
            "if errors.As(err, &me) { use(me.Code) }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Generics took over",
          "text": "Type parameters (Go 1.18+) replace many `interface{}` plus assertion patterns with compile-time safety."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Proverbs",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "'The bigger the interface, the weaker the abstraction' — Rob Pike",
            "'Accept interfaces, return structs'",
            "Flexible input, concrete and inspectable output"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Design: Small, and Where Used",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where To Declare It"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "In the consuming package, not beside the implementation",
            "The exact opposite of the Java convention",
            "Wait for a second implementation or a real test seam"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Naming And Size"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Method name plus `-er`: `Reader`, `Formatter`, `Notifier`",
            "Single-method interfaces dominate the stdlib",
            "`sort.Interface` is the fat outlier at three"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Interface",
            "Methods"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`error`",
              "1"
