          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Accidental `Stringer`",
          "items": [
            "Any type with `String() string` becomes one",
            "Every `%v` in the program changes at once",
            "Same hazard for `Error() string` on a value type"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The `String()` Recursion",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "func (p P) String() string {",
            "\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%v\", p) // infinite!",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A **stack overflow** at run time, never a compile error",
            "Fix: format the fields, not the value itself",
            "Or convert to a method-less local type first"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors And Assertions"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "#8 `errors.Is` for sentinel identity",
            "#8 `errors.As` to extract a concrete type from the chain",
            "#9 Forgetting comma-ok turns a mismatch into a panic",
            "#10 Refactor drift: guard with `var _ I = (*T)(nil)`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Use",
            "Note"
